</p>
<p>Two time intervals are given, but they&#8217;re not needed to solve the problem. The first question is asked between Bixley and Pixley; call that point <em>x</em>. The second question is asked between Pixley and Quixley; call that point <em>y</em>. The distance between <em>x</em> and <em>y</em> is 7 miles. The distance from <em>x</em> to Pixley is two-thirds the distance from Bixley to Pixley, and the distance from <em>y</em> to Pixley is two-thirds the distance between Pixley and Quixley. So the distance from <em>x</em> to <em>y</em>, 7 miles, is two-thirds the total distance, which must be 10.5 miles.</p>
